hadiths[271]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2733","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: Do you wish to exert yourselves in supplication? Say: ""O Allah, help us to thank You, remember You, and worship You in the best manner."
"2734","[AI-translation] Narrated from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, raised to the Prophet: Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it is carried upon the clouds. Allah, Majestic is His Majesty, says: By My Might and My Majesty, I shall surely aid you, even if after a time."
"2735","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it ascends to the heaven like a spark."
"2736","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas ibn Malik, raised to the Prophet: Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, even if he is a disbeliever, for there is no barrier before it."
"2737","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Gather, for I will recite to you a third of the Qur'an."" So those who gathered gathered. Then the Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came out and recited: ""Say: He is Allah, the One."" Then he went inside. Some of us said to others, ""I think news has come to him from heaven, and that is what made him go inside."" Then the Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came out and said: ""I said to you: I will recite to you a third of the Qur'an. Verily, it equals a third of the Qur'an."
"2738","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Call upon Allah, Exalted be He, while you are certain of the response, and know that Allah does not answer a supplication from a heart that is heedless and inattentive."
"2739","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: If you experience a pain, place your hand where you feel the pain and say: ""In the name of Allah (and by Allah), I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find of this pain of mine."" Then raise your hand, then repeat that an odd number of times."
"2740","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'A'ishah that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, used to gather his household and say: ""If distress or anguish afflicts any of you, let him say: 'Allah, Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him.'"
"2741","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When you enter the morning, say: ""O Allah! By You we enter the morning, and by You we enter the evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the resurrection."" And when you enter the evening, say: ""O Allah! By You we enter the evening, and by You we enter the morning, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the return."
"2742","[AI-translation] Munkadir: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and complained to him about terrifying dreams he saw in his sleep. He said: ""When you retreat to your bed, say: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His wrath and His punishment, and from the evil of His servants, and from the whisperings of the devils and that they should be present.'"
"2743","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aisha: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When one of you wishes, let him wish abundantly, for he is only asking his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."
"2744","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When an absent person supplicates for an absent person, the angel says to him: 'And for you is the like.'"
"2745","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira, raising it: ""When you are reminded of Allah, then stop."
"2746","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aisha: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When one of you asks, let him ask abundantly, for he is only asking his Lord."
"2747","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Irbad bin Sarikh: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaus, for it is the center of Paradise. A man among you says to his shepherd: 'Stick to the center of the valley, for it is the most fertile and the most lush.'"
"2748","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""When you hear the crowing of a rooster at night, ask Allah for His bounty (and turn to Him eagerly), for it saw an angel. And when you hear the braying of a donkey at night, seek refuge with Allah from Satan, for it saw a devil."
"2749","On the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa'id, who both bore witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When the servant says, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest,' Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, and I am the Greatest.' And when the servant says: 'There is no god but Allah alone,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me alone.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, He has no partner,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, and I have no partner.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, to Me belongs the dominion and to Me belongs all praise.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, and there is no power and no strength except with Me.' Whoever is granted these words at the time of his death, the Fire will not touch him."""
"2750","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you recite Al-Hamd (Praise be to Allah), recite Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Raheem (In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful), for it is the Mother of the Qur'an, the Mother of the Book, and the Seven Oft-Repeated, and Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Raheem is one of them."
"2751","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""When you pass by the gardens of Paradise, then graze."" He was asked: ""And what are the gardens of Paradise?"" He said: ""The circles of remembrance."
"2752","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Khawlah bint Hakim that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you stops at a resting place, let him say: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created.' For nothing will harm him until he departs from it."
"2753","[AI-translation] Qurashi that a man from the Ansar was afflicted by an ant bite, and he was directed to Al-Shifa' bint 'Abdullah who used to perform Ruqyah for ant bites. He came to her and asked her to perform Ruqyah on him, but she said: ""By Allah, I have not performed Ruqyah since I accepted Islam."" The Ansari man went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) and informed him of what Al-Shifa' had said. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) called Al-Shifa' and said: ""Present it to me."" She presented it to him, and he said: ""Perform Ruqyah on him, and teach it to Hafsah just as you taught her the Book."" In a narration: ""writing."
"2754","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to say: ""Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the neighbor of the residence, for the neighbor of the traveler, if he wishes, can depart."
"2755","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Aishah, marfu'an: ""Seek refuge in Allah the Almighty from the evil eye, for the evil eye is true."
"2756","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Prophet (peace be upon him) took her hand and pointed with her toward the moon and said: ""Seek refuge in Allah from this, for it is the darkening one when it sets."
"2757","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Umamah, marfu'an: ""The Greatest Name of Allah is in three surahs of the Qur'an: in Al-Baqarah, Aal 'Imran, and Ta-Ha."
"2758","[AI-translation] Ashja'i said: ""We used to perform Ruqyah during the pre-Islamic period. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What do you think about that?' He said: 'Present your Ruqyah to me. There is nothing wrong with Ruqyah as long as it does not involve Shirk.'"
"2759","[AI-translation] Jabir bin 'Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""The best dhikr is 'La ilaha illa Allah' and the best gratitude is 'Al-hamdulillah'."
"2760","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Imran bin Husain, marfu'an: ""The best of the servants of Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection are the praisers."
"2761","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Abbas, marfu'an: ""The best act of worship is supplication."
"2762","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ali, marfu'an: ""The best of what I and the prophets have said on the evening of Arafah is: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs the praise, and He is over all things competent."
"2763","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Abza, from his father, that the Prophet peace be upon him and his family omitted a verse, so when he finished praying he said: ""Is Ubayy among the people?"" Ubayy said: ""Was such-and-such a verse abrogated, or did you forget it?"" He said: ""Rather, I forgot it."
"2764","[AI-translation] Bara who said: A man recited Surah al-Kahf while he had a riding animal tied up, and the animal began to shy away. The man looked at a cloud or mist that had covered him, and he became frightened, so he went to the Prophet peace be upon him and his family. I said: Did the Prophet peace be upon him and his family name that man? He said: Yes. (He said: so he mentioned that to the Prophet peace be upon him) and he said: ""Read, O so-and-so! For it is tranquility that descended for the Quran, or with the Quran."
"2765","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas, marfu'an: ""Recite the Quran in seven ahruf, all of which are healing and sufficient."
"2766","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah bin Amr that the Prophet peace be upon him and his family said to him: ""Recite the Quran in forty..."" then in a month, then in twenty, then in fifteen, then in ten, then in seven. He said: it ended at seven."
"2767","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah bin Amr who said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! In how much time should I recite the Quran?"" He said: ""Recite it in a month."" I said: ""I am capable of more than that."" He said: ""Recite it in twenty-five... Recite it in twenty... Recite it in fifteen... Recite it in seven. He who recites it in less than three [days] will not understand it."
"2768","[AI-translation] Kindi, who said: Ibn Masud was teaching a man to recite, and the man recited (At-Tawbah: 60) without prolongation. Ibn Masud said: ""The Messenger of Allah peace be upon him and his family did not teach me to recite it like this."" He said: ""And how did he teach you to recite it, O Abu Abd al-Rahman?"" He said: ""Innama al-sadaqatu lil-fuqara'i wal-masakin (60)"" and he prolonged it."
"2769","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah peace be upon him and his family said: ""Recite Surah al-Baqarah in your houses, for Satan does not enter a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited."
"2770","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah peace be upon him and his family came out to us while we were reciting the Quran, and among us were a Bedouin and a non-Arab. He said: ""Recite, for all of it is good. And there will come a people who will straighten it like an arrow is straightened; they will rush it and not delay it."
"2771","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah peace be upon him said: ""Recite the Quran, for you will be rewarded for it. And indeed, I do not say that Alif-Lam-Mim is one letter; rather, Alif is ten, Lam is ten, and Mim is ten, so that is thirty."
"2772","[AI-translation] Bahili: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Recite the Quran, for it will come on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for its companions. Recite the two radiant ones, al-Baqarah and Surah Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two clouds, or two dark canopies, or as if they are two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading on behalf of their companions. Recite Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, abandoning it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot overcome it."
"2773","[AI-translation] Bajali: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Recite the Quran as long as your hearts are in agreement upon it, but if you disagree, then rise from it."
"2774","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Shibl al-Ansari that Muawiyah said to him: ""When you come to my pavilion, stand and inform me of what you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Recite the Quran, but do not eat with it, do not seek abundance with it, do not turn away from it, and do not go to excess in it.'"
"2775","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Shibl: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Recite the Quran, but do not go to excess in it, do not turn away from it, do not eat with it, and do not seek abundance with it."
"2776","[AI-translation] Narrated Uqbah bin Amir: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Recite the Mu'awwidhat after every prayer."
"2777","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas, raised to the Prophet: ""Increase your prayers upon me on Friday and the night of Friday. Whoever prays upon me once, Allah prays upon him ten times."
"2778","[AI-translation] Siddiq, raised to the Prophet: ""Increase prayers upon me, for Allah has appointed an angel at my grave. Whenever a man from my ummah prays upon me, that angel says to me: 'O Muhammad! So-and-so son of so-and-so prayed upon you just now.'"
"2779","[AI-translation] Narrated Aws bin Aws, raised to the Prophet: ""Increase your prayers upon me on Friday, for your prayers are presented to me."" They said: ""How are they presented to you when you have decayed?"" He said: ""Allah, the Exalted, has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets."
"2780","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Frequently say: 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah,' for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise."
"2781","Shall I not tell you of something which, if you adhere to it, you will catch up with those who have surpassed you, and no one will surpass you after it, and you will be the best among those around you, except for one who does the same as you? You glorify Allah (say Subḥān Allāh), praise Him (say Al-ḥamdu lillāh), and magnify Him (say Allāhu Akbar) thirty-three times after every prayer.On the authority of Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The poor came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""The people of wealth have taken the highest degrees and lasting bliss. They pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, but they have surplus wealth with which they perform Hajj and ʿUmrah, strive in the cause of Allah, and give charity."" He said: ... and he mentioned it (the narration).We differed among ourselves, so some of us said: ""We glorify thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times."" So I returned to him and he said: ""You say: Subḥān Allāh, Al-ḥamdu lillāh, Allāhu Akbar, until each of them reaches thirty-three."""
"2782","[AI-translation] Bahili, Sadi bin Ajlan, raised to the Prophet: ""Shall I not inform you of what is better or more abundant than your remembrance of Allah night and day, and day and night? It is that you say: 'Subhan Allah, the number of what He created; Subhan Allah, filling what He created; Subhan Allah, the number of what is in the earth and the heaven; Subhan Allah, filling what is in the heaven and the earth; Subhan Allah, filling what He created; Subhan Allah, the number of what He enumerated in His book; and Subhan Allah, filling everything.' And you say: 'Alhamdulillah' similarly."
"2783","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, was on a journey and alighted, and a man alighted beside him. He said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, turned and said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of the Quran?"" He said: He then recited to him: ""All praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"2784","[AI-translation] Narrated Sa'd: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: ""Shall I not inform you of something which, if distress or a trial from the trials of this world befalls a man among you and he supplicates with it, it will be lifted from him?"" It was said to him: ""Yes."" He said: ""The supplication of Dhun-Nun: 'There is no deity except You; exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers' (Al-Anbiya 87)."
"2785","[AI-translation] Narrated Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah: His father handed him over to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, to serve him. He said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, passed by me while I had prayed, and he nudged me with his foot and said: ""Shall I not direct you to a gate from the gates of Paradise? 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah.'"
"2786","[AI-translation] Narrated Shaddad bin Aws: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Shall I not direct you to the master of seeking forgiveness? 'O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no deity except You. You created me and I am Your servant (and the son of Your servant), and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge with You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favor upon me and I confess my sins, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins except You.' No one says it in the evening except that Paradise becomes due for him."
"2787","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: Fatimah came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, asking him for a servant and complaining of the hardship of work. He said: ""I do not have what you desire with us!"" He said: ""Shall I not direct you to what is better for you than a servant? You glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and exalt Allah thirty-four times when you take your resting place."
"2788","[AI-translation] Walid: I used to be frightened at night, so I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: ""I am frightened at night, so I take my sword and do not encounter anything except that I strike it with my sword."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Shall I not teach you words which the Trustworthy Spirit taught me?"" He said: ""Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no righteous or wicked person can surpass, from the evil of what descends from the sky and from the evil of what ascends in it, and from the evil of the trials of the night and the day, and from every night-comer, except a night-comer who comes with good, O Most Merciful!"
"2789","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet said: ""Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday, after the Asr prayer until the setting of the sun."
"2790","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Hold fast to: 'O Lord of Majesty and Honor.'"" Narrated from the hadith of......"
"2791","[AI-translation] Narrated a man from the Ansar: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say at the end of the prayer: ""O Allah, forgive me and accept my repentance, indeed You are the Accepter of repentance, the Forgiving"" (one hundred times)."
"2792","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! This is your little servant, so supplicate to Allah for him."" He said: ""O Allah, increase his wealth and his offspring, and prolong his life, and forgive him."" He said: ""My wealth multiplied and my life was prolonged until I felt shy before my family, (and my fruits ripened), and as for the fourth, meaning forgiveness."
"2793","[AI-translation] From Anas, who said: Umm Sulaim said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Supplicate to Allah for him,"" meaning Anas. He said: ""O Allah, increase his wealth and his progeny, and bless for him what You have bestowed upon him."
"2794","[AI-translation] From Abu Wa'il who said: A man came to Ali and said: ""O Commander of the Faithful! I have become unable to fulfill my mukatabah, so help me."" Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Shall I not teach you some words that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, taught me? Were you to have upon you [a debt] like the mountain of Sir of dinars, Allah would discharge it for you."" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Say: O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your unlawful, and enrich me by Your grace beyond anyone other than You."
"2795","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Amr: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, went out on the day of Badr with three hundred and fifteen [men]. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""O Allah, they are barefoot, so carry them. O Allah, they are unclothed, so clothe them. O Allah, they are hungry, so feed them."" So Allah granted him victory on the day of Badr, and when they returned, there was not a man among them except that he returned with a camel or two, and they were clothed and sated."
"2796","On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught her this supplication: ""O Allah, I ask You for all good, its immediate and its deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. And I seek refuge in You from all evil, its immediate and its deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Prophet asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil that Your servant and Prophet sought refuge in You from. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and that which brings one closer to it of word or deed, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and that which brings one closer to it of word or deed. And I ask You to make every decree You have decreed for me good."""
"2797","[AI-translation] From Murrah bin Abdullah, who said: A guest befell the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, so he sent to his wives seeking food from them, but found none with any of them. He said: ""O Allah, I ask You for Your grace and Your mercy, for none controls them but You."" A roasted sheep was then gifted to him, whereupon he said: ""This is from the grace of Allah, and we await the mercy."
"2798","[AI-translation] From Mus'ab: Sa'd used to enjoin five things, and he mentioned them from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he used to enjoin them: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from stinginess, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the most decrepit age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the world, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave."
"2799","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Among his supplications, peace be upon him, was: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor, and from a spouse who grays me before old age, and from a child who is arrogant against me, and from wealth that becomes a punishment for me, and from a deceitful companion whose eyes observe me and whose heart watches me; if he sees a good deed he buries it, and if he sees an evil deed he broadcasts it."
"2800","[AI-translation] From Zaid bin Arqam who said: I do not say to you except what the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to say. He used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness and cowardice and stinginess and senility, and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant my soul its piety and purify it; You are the best of those who purify it, You are its Guardian and its Master. O Allah! I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, and from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a supplication that is not answered."
"2801","[AI-translation] From Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""O Allah, Lord of Jibrail, Mika'il, and Lord of Israfil, I seek refuge in You from the heat of the Fire and from the punishment of the grave."
"2802","[AI-translation] He used to supplicate, saying: ""O Allah! Grant me enjoyment of my hearing and my sight, and make them survive me, and grant me victory over him who wrongs me, and exact my vengeance from him."" Narrated from a group of the Companions... and Abdullah bin Al-Sakhir, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2803","[AI-translation] From Fadalah bin Ubaid: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""O Allah, whoever believes in You and testifies that I am Your Messenger, make the meeting with You beloved to him, and make his passing easy for him, and decrease for him of the world. And whoever does not believe in You and does not testify that I am Your Messenger, do not make the meeting with You beloved to him, and do not make his passing easy for him, and increase for him of the world."
"2804","[AI-translation] Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""O Allah, there is no ease except in what You have made easy, and You make hardship easy if You will."
"2805","[AI-translation] Mu'awiyah said while on the pulpit: ""O Allah, none can withhold what You have given, and none can give what You have withheld, and the wealth of the wealthy is of no avail against You. Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding of the religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) upon this pulpit."
"2806","[AI-translation] Al-Aswad ibn Sari' reported: I was a poet, so I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have praised my Lord."" He said: ""Verily, your Lord loves praises, and you did not ask me for more than that."
"2807","[AI-translation] Ash'ari reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) commanded us to say when we enter the morning, when we enter the evening, and when we lie down on our beds: ""O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, You are the Lord of all things, and the angels bear witness that there is no god but You. We seek refuge in You from the evil of our souls, from the evil of Satan the accursed and his partnership, and from committing evil against ourselves or bringing it upon a Muslim."
"2808","[AI-translation] 'Aishah reported that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to perform Ruqyah by saying: ""Remove the harm, O Lord of mankind; in Your hand is the healing; none removes the distress but You."
"2809","[AI-translation] 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of words to Allah is for the servant to say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You.' And the most hateful of words to Allah is for a man to say to a man: 'Fear Allah,' and he replies: 'Upon yourself.'"
"2810","[AI-translation] 'Aishah reported, raising it to the Prophet: ""The best of people in recitation is the one who, when he recites, you see that he fears Allah."
"2811","[AI-translation] Ubayy ibn Ka'b reported that the Messenger of Allah said to him: ""Indeed, Allah has commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you."" He recited to him: ""Lam yakunilladhina kafaru..."" And he recited in it: ""Indeed, the religion with Allah is the upright Muslim way (al-Hanifiyyah al-Muslimah), not Judaism, nor Christianity, nor Zoroastrianism. Whoever does good will not have it denied."" And he recited to him: ""If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would desire a second, and if he had a second, he would desire a third..."" etc. (He said: Then he concluded it with what remained of it)."
"2812","On the authority of ʿAlī ibn Rabīʿah, who said: I was riding behind ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). When he placed his foot in the stirrup, he said: ""In the name of Allah."" When he settled upon the mount's back, he said: ""All praise is due to Allah"" three times, and ""Allah is the Greatest"" three times, then: ""Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it"" (Qurʾān 43:13). Then he said: ""There is no deity but You, glory be to You; indeed I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins except You."" Then he leaned to one side and laughed. I said: ""O Commander of the Faithful, what makes you laugh?"" He said: ""I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did just as I have done. I asked him just as you asked me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Indeed Allah marvels at the servant when he says: ""There is no deity but You, glory be to You; indeed I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins except You."" He says: ""My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives and punishes.""'"""
"2813","[AI-translation] Harith met 'Umar at 'Usfan, and 'Umar had appointed him over Makkah. He said: ""Whom have you appointed over the people of the valley?"" He said: ""Ibn Abza."" He said: ""And who is Ibn Abza?"" He said: ""A freed slave from our freed slaves."" He said: ""So you appointed a freed slave over them?"" He said: ""Indeed, he is a reciter of the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and he is knowledgeable of the laws of inheritance (al-fara'id)."" 'Umar said: ""Verily, your Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: 'Indeed, Allah raises people by this Book and lowers others by it.'"
"2814","[AI-translation] 'As reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, faith wears out in the heart of one of you just as a garment wears out, so ask Allah to renew the faith in your hearts."
"2815","[AI-translation] From Aishah, from Fatimah, marfu: ""Verily, Jibril used to review the Quran with me once every year, and he reviewed it with me twice this year. I see nothing but that my time has drawn near, and you are the first of my family to catch up with me. So fear Allah and be patient, for what an excellent predecessor I am for you."
"2816","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The best of the servants of Allah are those who watch the sun, the moon, the stars, and the shadows for the remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"2817","[AI-translation] Sakan al-Asadi, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon his wife and saw upon her a protective amulet of red [thread]. He cut it forcefully, then said: ""The family of Abdullah are rich beyond shirk."" And he said: ""Among what we memorized from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, is: 'Verily, incantations, amulets, and tiwalah are shirk.'"
"2818","[AI-translation] From Abdullah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Verily, incantations, amulets, and tiwalah are shirk."
"2819","On the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: A young man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Give me permission to commit fornication."" The people turned to him and rebuked him, saying: ""Stop! Stop!"" But he said: ""Bring him close."" So he came close to him, and he sat down. He said: ""Would you like it for your mother?"" He said: ""No, by Allah! May Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""Nor do people like it for their mothers."" He said: ""Would you like it for your daughter?"" He said: ""No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah! May Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""Nor do people like it for their daughters."" He said: ""Would you like it for your sister?"" He said: ""No, by Allah! May Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""Nor do people like it for their sisters."" He said: ""Would you like it for your paternal aunt?"" He said: ""No, by Allah! May Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""Nor do people like it for their paternal aunts."" He said: ""Would you like it for your maternal aunt?"" He said: ""No, by Allah! May Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""Nor do people like it for their maternal aunts."" Then he placed his hand on him and said: ""O Allah! Forgive his sin, purify his heart, and guard his chastity."" And after that, the young man never turned his attention to anything (of that nature)."
"2820","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Verily, this Quran was revealed upon seven letters, so recite it, there is no harm. But do not conclude a mention of mercy with punishment, nor a mention of punishment with mercy."
"2821","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, took a branch and shook it, but it did not shed its leaves. Then he shook it again, but it did not shed. Then he shook it, and it shed. He said: ""Verily, Subhan Allah, wal-hamdulillah, wa la ilaha illallah, wallahu Akbar shed sins just as this tree sheds its leaves."
"2822","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Buraidah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Abdullah ibn Qays, or the Ash'ari, was given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"2823","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar: We used to count for the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, in the gathering, saying: ""O Lord! Forgive me and accept my repentance. Verily, You are the Accepter of repentance, the Oft-Forgiving,"" one hundred times."
"2824","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Masud, mawquf and marfu: ""Verily, everything has a peak, and the peak of the Quran is Surat al-Baqarah. And verily, when the Shaytan hears Surat al-Baqarah, he leaves the house in which Surat al-Baqarah is recited."
"2825","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ: ""Indeed, Allah has angels who roam the earth, beyond the scribes of mankind, seeking out the people of remembrance. When they find a people remembering Allah, they call out: 'Come to your object of pursuit!' So they come and surround them up to the lowest heaven. Then Allah asks—though He knows best: 'What do My servants say?' They reply: 'They glorify You, magnify You, and remember You.' He says: 'Have they seen Me?' They say: 'No.' He says: 'How would it be if they saw Me?' They say: 'If they saw You, they would be even more intense in glorifying, magnifying, and remembering You.' He says: 'What do they ask for?' They say: 'They ask for Paradise.' He says: 'Have they seen it?' They say: 'No.' He says: 'How would it be if they saw it?' They say: 'If they saw it, they would be even more eager for it and more intense in seeking it.' He says: 'From what do they seek refuge?' They say: 'From the Fire.' He says: 'Have they seen it?' They say: 'No.' He says: 'How would it be if they saw it?' They say: 'If they saw it, they would flee from it even more intensely and fear it even more severely.' He says: 'I bear witness to you that I have forgiven them.' One of the angels says: 'Among them is so-and-so, a sinner, who did not intend to join them but came only for some need.' He says: 'They are the people such that their companion will not be wretched.'"""
"2826","[AI-translation] Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Among what you recite of the majesty of Allah are: Tasbih, Tahlil, and Tahmid. They fold around the Throne, having a buzzing like the buzzing of bees, mentioning their companion. Would not one of you love that he has, or rather always has, someone who mentions him?"
"2827","Abu Qays, the freed slave of Amr ibn al-As, narrated: Amr ibn al-As heard a man reciting a verse from the Quran. He asked: ""Who taught you this?"" The man replied: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" Amr said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me this verse differently."" So they both went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). One of them said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Such-and-such verse,"" then he recited it. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Thus it was revealed."" Then the other said: ""O Messenger of Allah!"" and he recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He asked: ""Is it not thus, O Messenger of Allah?"" He replied: ""Thus it was revealed."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this Quran was revealed in seven modes (ahruf), so whichever of them you recite, you have done well (and in another narration: you have hit the mark). And do not dispute concerning it, for disputing about it is disbelief."""
"2828","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I saw in a dream as if I was under a tree, and as if the tree was reciting: (Sad), and when it reached the prostration verse, it prostrated, and it said in its prostration: ""O Allah, write for me a reward by it, and remove from me a burden by it, and create for me gratitude by it, and accept it from me as You accepted the prostration of Your servant Dawud."" So when morning came, I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of that. He said: ""Did you prostrate, O Abu Sa'id?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""You were more deserving of prostration than the tree."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surah Sad until he reached the prostration verse, and he said in his prostration what the tree had said in its prostration."
"2829","[AI-translation] Narrated from `Uqbah ibn `Amir, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: Verses have been revealed to me the likes of which have never been seen: ""Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,"" to the end of the Surah, and ""Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,"" to the end of the Surah."
"2830","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: You will not return to anything better than that which came forth from it, meaning the Quran."
"2831","[AI-translation] Narrated from `Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from his father: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came one day and joy was visible on his face. They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We certainly see joy on your face."" He said: ""An angel came to me and said: 'O Muhammad! Would it not please you that your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: No one from your Ummah sends blessings upon you except that I send blessings upon him ten times, and no one from your Ummah sends peace upon you except that I send peace upon him ten times?'"" He replied: ""Yes."
"2832","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I indeed recognize the voices of the Ash`arin company by the Quran when they enter at night, and I recognize their dwellings by their voices with the Quran at night, though I did not see their dwellings when they alighted by day. And among them is Hakim who, when he encountered the cavalry—or he said: the enemy—said to them: 'My companions order you to look at them.'"
"2833","On the authority of Sulayman ibn Surad, he said: Two men reviled each other in the presence of the Prophet (peace be upon him). One of them became angry and his face turned red. The Prophet (peace be upon him) looked at him and said: ""I know a word which, if he said it, would remove what he feels. If he said: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan.'"" A man who heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) went to that man and said: ""Do you know what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) just said?"" He said: ""I know a word which, if he said it, would remove what he feels. If he said: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan.'"" The man said to him: ""Do you see me as insane?"""
"2834","[AI-translation] Khudri: A man came to him and said: ""Advise me."" He said: ""You have asked about what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) before you. He said: 'I advise you to have taqwa of Allah, for it is the head of all things, and upon you is Jihad, for it is the monasticism of Islam, and upon you is the remembrance of Allah and the recitation of the Quran, for it is your spirit in the heaven and your remembrance on the earth.'"
"2835","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) intending a journey, and he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Advise me."" He said: ""I advise you to have taqwa of Allah, and to proclaim the Takbir upon every elevated place."
"2836","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn `Abbas, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him): The allies of Allah are those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered."
"2837","On the authority of Abu Dharr: Some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said to the Prophet ﷺ: ""O Messenger of Allah! The people of wealth have gone off with the rewards. They pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they give charity from their excess wealth."" He said: ""Has Allah not given you something to give in charity? Verily, every tasbihah is a charity, every takbirah is a charity, every tahmidah is a charity, every tahlilah is a charity, enjoining good is a charity, forbidding evil is a charity, and in the sexual act of one of you there is a charity."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, when one of us fulfills his desire, will he have a reward in that?"" He said: ""Do you not see that if he were to put it in the unlawful, would he have a sin upon him? So likewise, if he puts it in the lawful, he will have a reward."""
"2838","[AI-translation] Narrated from Mus`ab ibn Sa`d: My father narrated to me, saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and he said: ""Is one of you incapable of earning a thousand good deeds each day?"" A questioner from among those seated asked him: ""How can one of us earn a thousand good deeds?"" He said: ""He says Tasbih a hundred times, so a thousand good deeds are recorded for him, or a thousand sins are erased from him."
"2839","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Salam Sulami, the freed client of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Excellent! Excellent!""—and he gestured with his hand to five—""How heavy they are in the Balance: Subhan Allah, and Al-hamdu lillah, and La ilaha illa Allah, and Allahu Akbar, and the righteous child who passes away belonging to the Muslim, so he hopes for his reward."
"2840","On the authority of Ibn Mas'ud, he said: While Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) was praying near the House (Ka'bah), Abu Jahl and his companions were sitting, and a camel had been slaughtered the previous day. Abu Jahl said: ""Which of you will go to the entrails of the camel of Banu so-and-so, take it, and place it on Muhammad's shoulders when he prostrates?"" So the most wretched of the people got up and took it. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) prostrated, he placed it between his shoulders. He said: They laughed so hard that they leaned on one another, while I was standing watching. If I had the power, I would have thrown it off the back of Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) was prostrating, not raising his head, until a person went and informed Fatimah. She came, and she was a young girl, and threw it off him. Then she turned to them, insulting them. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished his prayer, he raised his voice and supplicated against them. He would supplicate three times and ask three times. Then he said: ""O Allah, deal with Quraysh"" (three times). When they heard his voice, their laughter vanished and they feared his supplication. Then he said: ""O Allah, deal with Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, Al-Walid ibn 'Uqbah, Umayyah ibn Khalaf, 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt,"" and he mentioned the seventh but I did not memorize it. By Him Who sent Muhammad (peace be upon him) with the truth, I saw those he named slain on the day of Badr, then they were dragged to the well, the well of Badr."
"2841","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: We were sitting in the mosque reciting the Quran, when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) entered and greeted us with peace. We returned the greeting of peace upon him, then he said: ""Learn the Book of Allah, take hold of it, and beautify your voices with it. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is more prone to slipping away than a young camel from its tether."
"2842","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from poverty, scarcity, and humiliation, and from being wronged or wronging."
"2843","[AI-translation] As Al-Thaqafi reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) who said: The gates of heaven are opened in the middle of the night, and a caller calls out: ""Is there any supplicant so that he may be answered? Is there any asker so that he may be given? Is there any distressed person so that relief may be granted to him?"" No Muslim remains who supplicates with a supplication except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, answers him, except an adulteress who seeks with her private part, or a tax collector."
"2844","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, that the Prophet ﷺ recited the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in [the story of] Ibrāhīm: ""My Lord, indeed they have led astray many among the people. So whoever follows me - then he is of me"" (Qurʾān 14:36). And ʿĪsā, peace be upon him, said: ""If You punish them, indeed they are Your servants; but if You forgive them, indeed You are the Exalted in Might, the Wise"" (Qurʾān 5:118).Then he raised his hands and said: ""O Allah! My Ummah, my Ummah,"" and he wept.Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ""O Jibrīl! Go to Muḥammad — and your Lord knows best — and ask him: 'What makes you weep?'""So Jibrīl, peace be upon him, came to him and asked him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed him of what he had said, though He is most knowing.Allah said: ""O Jibrīl! Go to Muḥammad and say: 'Indeed We will please you concerning your Ummah and We will not displease you.'"""
"2845","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, raised to the Prophet: Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of a parent, the supplication of a fasting person, and the supplication of a traveler."
"2846","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) who said: There are three whose supplication Allah does not reject: the one who remembers Allah abundantly, the supplication of the oppressed, and the just imam."
"2847","Abu al-Tayyah narrated: A man asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbash: ""How did the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) fare when the devils nearly overpowered him?"" He said: ""The devils came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) from the valleys and descended upon him from the mountains, and among them was a devil with a flame of fire wanting to burn the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) with it."" He said: ""He was terrified."" Ja'far said: ""I think he said: 'He began to retreat.'"" He said: ""And Gabriel (peace be upon him) came and said: 'O Muhammad! Say:' He said: 'What should I say?' He said: 'Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah which neither the righteous nor the wicked can surpass, from the evil of what He created, scattered, and originated; and from the evil of what descends from the heaven and from the evil of what ascends therein; and from the evil of what He scattered in the earth and from the evil of what emerges from it; and from the evil of the trials of night and day; and from the evil of every night visitor except a visitor who comes with good, O Most Merciful!'"" So the fire of the devils was extinguished and Allah the Mighty and Majestic defeated them."
"2848","[AI-translation] Alqamah bin Qays said: I was a man to whom Allah had given a good voice for the Quran, so Abdullah bin Mas'ud would send for me and I would recite to him. He said: When I finished my recitation, he would say: ""Give us more of this, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A good voice is an adornment for the Quran."
"2849","[AI-translation] Abu Wa'il said: Ibn Mas'ud addressed us and said: ""How can you command me to recite according to the recitation of Zayd bin Thabit after I recited from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) seventy-odd surahs, while Zayd was with the boys having two braids?"
"2850","[AI-translation] Mus'ab bin Sa'd reported from his father, raised to the Prophet: The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it."
"2851","[AI-translation] Uthman bin Affan reported, raised to the Prophet: The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it."
"2852","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: Verily, the world is cursed; cursed is what is in it except the remembrance of Allah, what is allied to it, and a scholar or a learner."
"2853","[AI-translation] Al-Bara' said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adorn the Quran with your voices, for a good voice increases the Quran in beauty."
"2854","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Subhan Allah, Alhamdulillah, La ilaha illallah, and Allahu Akbar are from the enduring good deeds."
"2855","Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me, and I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have grown old and become weak"" — or as she said: ""Command me to do a deed that I can perform while sitting."" He said: ""Glorify Allah (say Subḥān Allāh) one hundred times, for it will equal for you one hundred necks (slaves) that you free from the descendants of Ismāʿīl. And praise Allah (say Al-ḥamdu lillāh) one hundred times, it will equal for you one hundred saddled and bridled horses that you ride in the cause of Allah. And magnify Allah (say Allāhu Akbar) one hundred times, for it will equal for you one hundred sacrificial camels adorned and accepted. And say Lā ilāha illā Allāh (Tahlīl) one hundred times."" Ibn Khalaf said: ""I think he said: 'It fills what is between the heaven and the earth, and no deed will be raised on that day for anyone except one who comes with the like of what you came with.'"""
"2856","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The Mufarridun have preceded."" They asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! And who are the Mufarridun?"" He said: ""Those who are absorbed in the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"2857","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Buraidah, from his father: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) reciting in prayer: ""If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would seek a second one, and if he were given a second, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust."
"2858","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah (bin Masud), marfu'an: ""Surah Tabarak is the protector from the torment of the grave."
"2859","[AI-translation] Narrated from Uqbah, marfu'an: ""A people will emerge from my Ummah who will drink the Quran as they drink water."
"2860","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have grown gray-haired?"" He said: ""Hud, Al-Waqi'ah, Al-Mursalat, 'Amma Yatasa'alun, and Idhash-Shamsu Kuwwirat have made me gray-haired."
"2861","On the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, who said: Ibn Ubayy narrated to me that his father informed him: that they had a storage vessel (jurn) containing dates, and his father used to check on it and found it decreasing. So he guarded it, and behold, there was a creature resembling a young man who had reached puberty. He said: I greeted him, and he returned the greeting. I said: ""Who are you? A jinn or a human?"" He said: ""A jinn."" I said: ""Give me your hand."" He gave me his hand, and behold, it was a dog's hand, with a dog's hair. I said: ""Is this how the jinn are created?"" He said: ""The jinn know that there is none among them stronger than I."" His father said to him: ""What made you do what you did?"" He said: ""We heard that you are a man who loves charity, so we wanted to partake of your food."" His father said: ""What protects us from you?"" He said: ""This verse: the Verse of the Throne (Āyat al-Kursī)."" Then he went in the morning to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: ""The wicked one spoke the truth."""
"2862","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: ""Send blessings upon the prophets and messengers of Allah, for Allah sent them just as He sent me."
"2863","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Send blessings upon me, for your blessings upon me are a purification for you, and ask Allah to grant me the Wasilah."
"2864","[AI-translation] Mazini: Two Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). One of them said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Which of the people is best?"" He said: ""Tuba for the one whose life is long and whose deeds are good."" The other said: ""Which deed is best?"" He said: ""The best deed is that you leave the world while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah."
"2865","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Amr: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the spoil of the gatherings of Dhikr?"" He said: ""The spoil of the gatherings of Dhikr is Paradise."
"2866","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted be He, said: ""O son of Adam! If you remember Me when you are alone, I will remember you when you are alone. And if you remember Me in an assembly, I will remember you in an assembly better than those in whom you remember Me."
"2867","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas bin Malik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Allah, Exalted be He, said: ""O son of Adam! As long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I will forgive you for what is in you, and I care not. O son of Adam! If your sins were to reach the clouds of the sky and then you seek My forgiveness, I will forgive you, and I care not. O son of Adam! If you were to come to Me with an earth full of sins and then meet Me not associating anything with Me, I would come to you with an earth full of forgiveness."
"2868","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Salman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: A man said, ""Praise be to Allah abundantly."" The angel considered it too great to write, so he consulted his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, concerning it. It was said to him: ""Write it as My servant said: abundantly."
"2869","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn Abbas who said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace be upon him), ""Call upon your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold, and we will believe in you."" He said, ""Will you do so?"" They said, ""Yes."" So he supplicated, and Jibril came to him and said, ""Your Lord conveys peace to you and says: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold for them tomorrow, and whoever disbelieves after that among them, I will punish him with a punishment I will not inflict upon anyone among the worlds. And if you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance and mercy."" He said, ""Rather, the door of repentance and mercy."
"2870","[AI-translation] Ashja'i, from his father (Tariq bin Ashim), that he heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) when a man came to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How should I say when I ask my Lord?"" He said: ""Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy upon me, grant me well-being, and provide for me."" And he gathered his fingers except the thumb, for indeed these gather for you your worldly life and your Hereafter."
"2871","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Instruct me with something to say when I enter the morning and when I enter the evening."" He said, ""Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Sovereign of all things. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, the evil of the Shaitan, and his Shirk. Say it when you enter the morning, and when you enter the evening, and when you take to your bed."
"2872","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, teach me something good."" The Prophet ﷺ took him by the hand and said: ""Say: Subḥānallāh (Glory be to Allah), wal-ḥamdu lillāh (All praise is due to Allah), wa lā ilāha illallāh (There is no deity but Allah), wallāhu akbar (Allah is the Greatest)."" The Bedouin counted them on his fingers and left. After a while, he returned, and the Prophet ﷺ smiled. He said: ""The poor man reflected."" He came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Subḥānallāh, wal-ḥamdu lillāh, wa lā ilāha illallāh, wallāhu akbar — this is for Allah; so what is for me?"" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""O Bedouin! When you say: Subḥānallāh, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Al-ḥamdu lillāh, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Lā ilāha illallāh, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Allāhu akbar, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Allāhumma ighfir lī (O Allah, forgive me), Allah says: 'I have done so.' When you say: Allāhumma arḥimnī (O Allah, have mercy on me), Allah says: 'I have done so.' When you say: Allāhumma arzuqnī (O Allah, provide for me), Allah says: 'I have done so.'"" The Bedouin then counted seven on his fingers and departed."
"2873","Abu al-Tayyah narrated: I said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbash al-Tamimi, who was a very old man: ""Did you meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deal with the night when the devils nearly overwhelmed him?"" He said: ""The devils descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that night from the valleys and mountain passes, and among them was a devil holding a flame of fire in his hand, wanting to burn the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Gabriel, peace be upon him, descended to him and said: 'O Muhammad! Say:' I said: 'And what should I say?' He said: 'Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah which neither the righteous nor the wicked can surpass, from the evil of what He created, scattered, and originated; and from the evil of what descends from the heaven and from the evil of what ascends therein; and from the evil of what He scattered in the earth and what emerges from it; and from the evil of the trials of the night and day; and from the evil of every visitor except a visitor who comes with good, O Most Merciful!' He said: So their fire was extinguished and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, defeated them."""
"2874","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Say: O you disbelievers"" equals a quarter of the Qur'an."
"2875","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Aisha who said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What if I know which night is the Night of Decree, what should I say in it?"" He said, ""Say: (and in a narration: you should say) O Allah! You are Pardoning, You love pardoning, so pardon me."
"2876","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Jabir from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: ""The Qur'an is an intercessor, and its intercession is accepted. Whoever puts it ahead of him, it will lead him to Paradise; and whoever puts it behind his back, it will drive him into the Fire."
"2877","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Awf bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The storytellers are of three types: a commander, one who is commanded, or a conceited one."
"2878","[AI-translation] From Anas: Whenever he, peace be upon him and his family, exerted himself in supplication for someone, he would say: ""May Allah impose upon you the prayer of a righteous people, who stand the night in prayer and fast the day, who are neither sinners nor wicked."
"2879","[AI-translation] Bara' ibn 'Azib who said: Whenever he, peace be upon him and his family, intended to sleep, he would place his hand under his right cheek and say: ""O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants."" It is also reported that..."
"2880","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, whenever he intended to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, would perform ablution, and if he intended to eat (while in a state of major ritual impurity), he would wash his hands."
"2881","[AI-translation] Mundhir: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, whenever he intended to enter a town, would not enter it until he said: ""O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, Lord of the devils and what they lead astray. I ask You for its good and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it."
"2882","[AI-translation] Akwa', who said: Whenever the wind became fierce, he, peace be upon him and his family, would say: ""O Allah, make it fertilizing, not barren."
"2883","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah: Whenever he, peace be upon him and his family, entered the morning, he would say: ""O Allah! By You we have entered the morning, and by You we have entered the evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the resurrection."" And when he entered the evening, he would say: ""O Allah! By You we have entered the evening, and by You we have entered the morning, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the destination."
"2884","[AI-translation] Bara' ibn 'Azib, who said: Whenever the Prophet, peace be upon him, retired to his bed, he would sleep on his right side, then say: ""O Allah, I have surrendered my soul to You, and directed my face to You, and entrusted my affair to You, and taken shelter with You, out of longing and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I have believed in Your Book which You revealed, and in Your Prophet whom You sent."" And he, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever says them and then dies during his night, dies upon the fitrah."
"2885","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, who said: Whenever an affair distressed him, he, peace be upon him and his family, would say: ""O Ever-Living! O Self-Subsisting! By Your mercy I seek help."
"2886","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, who said: Whenever he, peace be upon him and his family, supplicated (meaning: for rain), he would turn the backs of his hands to face his face."
"2887","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, who said: Whenever he, peace be upon him and his family, saw something he loved, he would say: ""Praise is to Allah, by Whose grace good deeds are completed."" And whenever he saw something he disliked, he would say: ""Praise is to Allah in every situation."
"2888","[AI-translation] Talhah bin Ubaidullah said: When he (peace be upon him and his family) saw the new moon, he would say: ""O Allah, let it appear upon us with blessing, faith, safety, and Islam. My Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"2889","[AI-translation] From Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace be upon him), whenever something alarmed him, would say: ""He is Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him."
"2890","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah said: When he (peace be upon him and his family) was on a journey and reached the pre-dawn hours, he would say: ""A hearer has heard our praise of Allah and His excellent favor upon us. Our Lord, accompany us and bestow upon us, seeking refuge in Allah from the Fire."
"2891","[AI-translation] Anas said: When a strong wind blew, he (peace be upon him and his family) would say: ""O Allah, I ask You for the good of what it has been sent with, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it has been sent with."
"2892","[AI-translation] Khatmi said: When he (peace be upon him and his family) bade farewell to an army, he would say: ""I entrust Allah with your religion, your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds."
"2893","[AI-translation] Shahr bin Hawshab said: I said to Umm Salamah: O Mother of the Believers! What was the most frequent supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) when he was with you? She said: His most frequent supplication was: ""O Turner of the hearts, keep my heart firm upon Your religion."" He was asked about that, and he said: ""There is no son of Adam except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; whoever He wills, He keeps firm, and whoever He wills, He causes to deviate."
"2894","On the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: There was a man (from the Jews) who used to visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), (and he trusted him). So he tied knots for him and placed them in the well of a man from the Ansar. (He fell ill because of that for several days) (and in the narration of Aisha: six months). Then two angels came to visit him. One sat at his head and the other at his feet. One of them said: ""Do you know what ails him?"" The other said: ""So-and-so, who (used to) visit him, tied knots for him and threw them into the well of so-and-so the Ansari. If a man were sent to him and he took the knots from it, he would find the water had turned yellow."" (Then Gabriel came to him and revealed to him Al-Mu'awwidhatayn [Surah Al-Falaq and Surah An-Nas] and said: ""A man from the Jews has bewitched you, and the magic is in the well of so-and-so."" He said:) So he sent a man (and in another narration: he sent Ali, may Allah be pleased with him) (and he found the water had turned yellow). He took the knots (and brought them). (He ordered him to untie the knots and recite a verse.) So he untied them, (and he began to recite and untie.) (And every time he untied a knot, he found relief from that.) So he was cured. (And in the other narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) stood up as if he had been released from a tether.) And the man used to visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) after that, but he did not mention anything of it to him, nor did he reproach him (at all until he died)."
"2895","Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to increase in saying in his final days: ""Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him, I seek forgiveness from Allah and I repent to Him."" (Aisha said:) So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Why do I see you increasing in saying: 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him, I seek forgiveness from Allah and I repent to Him?'"" He said: ""My Lord informed me that I would see a sign in my Ummah, and He commanded me that when I see that sign, I should glorify Him with His praise and seek His forgiveness. So I have seen it: 'When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest (1), and you see the people entering into the religion of Allah in multitudes (2), then glorify with the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness. Indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance (3).' (An-Nasr)"""
"2896","[AI-translation] From Ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), he said: The former scripture used to be revealed from one gate upon one letter, and the Quran was revealed from seven gates upon seven letters."
"2897","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah said: Among his (peace be upon him) supplications was: ""O Allah, forgive me for what I have sent forth and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public, and what You are more aware of than I am. You are the Advancer and the Delayer; there is no god but You."
"2898","[AI-translation] Aishah said: He (peace be upon him) would not recite the Quran in less than three (nights)."
"2899","[AI-translation] From Jabir: He (peace be upon him) would not sleep until he recited: ""Alif-Lam-Mim. The Revelation"" (As-Sajdah) and ""Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the Dominion"" (Al-Mulk)."
"2900","[AI-translation] 'A'ishah said: He (peace be upon him and his family) would not sleep until he recited (al-Zumar) and (Banu Isra'il)."
"2901","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) would use his right side as a pillow upon sleeping, then say: ""My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants."
"2902","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) that he used to supplicate: ""O Allah, protect me through Islam standing, and protect me through Islam sitting, and protect me through Islam sleeping, and do not let any envier rejoice at my misfortune. O Allah, I ask You for every good whose storehouse is in Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from every evil whose storehouse is in Your hand."
"2903","[AI-translation] 'Abdullah bin 'Umar said: He (peace be upon him) used to supplicate with these words: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from overwhelming debt, the overwhelming enemy, and the rejoicing of enemies."
"2904","[AI-translation] 'A'ishah said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to remember Allah at all his times."
"2905","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Abza from his father who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to (teach us), when one of us reached the morning, (that he should) say: ""We have reached the morning upon the fitrah of Islam, the word of sincerity, the religion of our Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him and his family), and the millah of our father Ibrahim, a hanif (muslim), and he was not of the mushrikin."
"2906","[AI-translation] 'A'ishah said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to seek refuge with these words: ""(O Allah, Lord of mankind) remove the harm and cure, for You are the Healer. There is no cure but Your cure, a cure that leaves no sickness."" When he became seriously ill in the sickness he died from, I took his hand and began to wipe him (with it) and say it, but he withdrew his hand from my hand and said: ""O Allah, forgive me and join me with the Highest Companion."" She said: So this was the last of his speech I heard (peace be upon him)."
"2907","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: He (peace be upon him and his family) would recite:"
"2908","[AI-translation] 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to say when he intended to sleep: ""O Allah! Originator of the heavens and the earth! Knower of the unseen and the seen! You are the Lord of everything and the God of everything. I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, You have no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and messenger, and the angels bear witness. O Allah! I seek refuge in You from Satan and his shirk, and I seek refuge in You lest I commit a sin against myself or direct it against a Muslim."
"2909","[AI-translation] Zubayr said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to say at the end of the prayer, when he said salam, before he would stand, raising his voice with it: ""There is no god but Allah, alone, He has no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is able to do all things. There is no power and no strength except by Allah. There is no god but Allah, (and) we worship none but Him. His is the favor, His is the grace, and His is the good praise. There is no god but Allah, making the religion sincere to Him, even if the disbelievers dislike it."
"2910","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah reported that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say in his supplication: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the evil neighbor in the permanent abode, for the neighbor of the desert moves away."
"2911","[AI-translation] Najm written in front of him, and when he reached the prostration, he prostrated, and we prostrated with him, and the inkwell and the pen prostrated."
"2912","[AI-translation] Khudri reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The Book of Allah is the rope of Allah extended from the heaven to the earth."
"2913","[AI-translation] From 'Ali, marfu': ""Every supplication is withheld until one invokes blessings upon the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family)."
"2914","[AI-translation] 'Ata' bin Abi Rabah reported: I saw Jabir bin 'Abdullah and Jabir bin 'Umair al-Ansari shooting arrows. One of them grew tired and sat down, so the other said to him: ""Are you tired? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: Everything that is not the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is (idle talk and) amusement or distraction, except for four traits: a man walking between two targets, training his horse, playing with his family, and learning to swim."
"2915","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Abbas reported from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""The words of relief are: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Most Great. There is no god but Him, the Lord of the seven heavens and the Lord of the Magnificent Throne."
"2916","[AI-translation] Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""For me to sit with a group of people remembering Allah, the Exalted, from the morning prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four from the offspring of Isma'il. And for me to sit with a group of people remembering Allah from the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four."
"2917","[AI-translation] Anas bin Malik reported: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) heard a man saying: ""O Allah! To You is praise, there is no god but You alone, You have no partner, the Bestower of gifts, Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Lord of Majesty and Honor!"" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""You have asked Allah by His Greatest Name: which, when He is invoked by it, He answers, and when He is asked by it, He gives."
"2918","[AI-translation] Jabir reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) went out to his companions and recited Surah Ar-Rahman to them from beginning to end, but they remained silent. He said: ""I recited it to the jinn on the night of the jinn, and they were more responsive than you. Whenever I came to His saying: 'So which of the favors of your Lord would you deny?' they said: 'We do not deny any of Your favors, our Lord, and to You is praise.'"
"2919","[AI-translation] Juwairiyah reported: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) left her company early in the morning after he prayed the morning prayer, while she was in her place of prayer. Then he returned after the sun had risen while she was still sitting there, and he said: ""Are you still in the same state as when I left you?"" She said: ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I have said four words three times after you left, which if weighed against what you have said since today, would outweigh them: 'Glory is to Allah and praise is to Him, equal to the number of His creation, His pleasure, the weight of His Throne, and the ink of His words.'"
"2920","[AI-translation] Narrated Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We used to recite during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): ""If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold and silver, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."
"2921","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Mas'ud (marfu'an): I met Ibrahim on the night I was taken on the Night Journey, and he said: ""O Muhammad! Convey greetings of peace to your Ummah from me, and inform them that Paradise has good soil and sweet water, and that it is a flat plain, and its plants are: 'Subhan Allah, wal-hamdu lillah, wa la ilaha illa Allah, wallahu Akbar' (and 'la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah')."
"2922","Anas ibn Malik reported: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'ba!"" He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: ""Hypocrisy, hypocrisy!"" He said: ""Do you not testify that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" They said: ""Yes, indeed."" He said: ""That is not hypocrisy."" Then they returned a second time and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'ba!"" He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: ""Hypocrisy, hypocrisy!"" He said: ""Do you not testify that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" They said: ""Yes, indeed."" He said: ""That is not hypocrisy."" Then they returned a third time and said the like of that, so he said to them: ""That is not hypocrisy."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! When we are with you, we are in a certain state, but when we leave your presence, worldly affairs and our families occupy us."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""If you were to remain, when you leave me, in the same state in which you are when you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you in the streets of Medina."""
"2923","[AI-translation] Narrated Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""If the Qur'an were placed in a leather hide and then thrown into the fire, it would not burn."
"2924","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: The wife of Ṣafwān ibn al-Muʿaṭṭal came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while we were with him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My husband Ṣafwān ibn al-Muʿaṭṭal beats me when I pray, breaks my fast when I fast, and does not perform the Fajr prayer until the sun rises."" Ṣafwān was present with him. He asked him about what she had said. He replied: ""O Messenger of Allah! As for her saying that I beat her when she prays, she recites two sūrahs, so I forbade her from that."" He said: ""If it were a single sūrah, it would suffice the people."" ""As for her saying that I break her fast, she fasts while I am a young man and I cannot restrain myself."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on that day: ""A woman must not fast except with her husband's permission."" ""As for her saying that I do not pray until the sun rises, we are a household known for this; we hardly wake up until the sun rises."" He said: ""When you wake up, then pray."""
"2925","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, and he recited this verse: ""Return to your lord and ask him what is the matter with the women who cut their hands. Indeed, my Lord is knowing of their plan."" [Yusuf: 50] The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""If I were him, I would have hastened the answer and would not have sought an excuse."
"2926","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that a group of three men from Banu Udhra came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will take care of them?"" Talha said: ""I will."" So they stayed with Talha. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and one of them went out in it and was martyred. Then he sent another expedition, and another of them went out in it and was martyred. Then the third died on his bed. Talha said: ""I saw these three who were with me in Paradise. I saw the one who died on his bed ahead of them, and I saw the one who was martyred last next to him, and I saw the one who was martyred first as the last of them."" He said: ""This caused me concern."" He said: ""So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What did you find objectionable about that? None is more excellent in the sight of Allah than a believer who is granted a long life in Islam for his glorification, magnification, and declaration of the oneness of Allah."""
"2927","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""No servant seeks refuge from the Fire seven times in a day, except that the Fire says: 'O Lord, your servant so-and-so has sought refuge with You from me, so grant him refuge.' And no servant asks Allah for Paradise seven times in a day, except that Paradise says: 'O Lord, your servant so-and-so has asked me for it, so enter him into Paradise.'"
"2928","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""No person is ever afflicted with anxiety and grief, and then says: 'O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant. My forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed, and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or taught to any of Your creation, or revealed in Your Book, or preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the spring of my heart and the light of my chest, a departure for my sorrow and a release for my anxiety,' except that Allah will remove his anxiety and grief and replace them with relief."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, should we not learn it?"" He said: ""Yes, whoever hears it should learn it."""
"2929","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came to us while we were sitting, and he said: ""I have never woken up in the morning except that I sought forgiveness from Allah in it one hundred times."
"2930","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: ""Which speech is best?"" He said: ""That which Allah has chosen for His servants: 'Subhan Allah wa bihamdih' (Glory be to Allah and His praise)."
"2931","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah (marfu'an): ""No people sit in a gathering without remembering Allah in it, except it is a source of regret for them, and no man walks a path without remembering Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, except it is a source of regret for him, and no man retires to his bed without remembering Allah, except it is a source of regret for him."
"2932","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah (marfu'an): ""No people sit in a gathering without remembering Allah in it and without sending blessings upon their Prophet, except it is a source of regret for them; if He wills, He may punish them, and if He wills, He may forgive them."
"2933","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah (marfu'an): He said, ""No people sit in a gathering remembering Allah in it, except that the angels surround them, mercy envelops them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those who are with Him."
"2934","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas, raised to the Prophet: No people sit remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except that a caller from the heaven calls out to them: Rise up forgiven, your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds."
"2935","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: No people sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and send blessings upon the Prophet, except that it will be a source of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection, even if they enter Paradise as a reward."
"2936","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: He said: There is no one who sends peace upon me except that Allah returns my soul to me until I return the peace upon him."
"2937","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There is no supplication that a servant calls upon better than: O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"2938","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Abd Allah bin Mughaffal, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: No people gather in a gathering and then disperse without remembering Allah, except that gathering will be a source of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."
"2939","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn 'Amr, raised to the Prophet: No people sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah, except that they will see it as a source of regret on the Day of Resurrection."
"2940","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: No people rise from a gathering in which they do not remember Allah, except that they rise from something like the carcass of a donkey, and it will be a source of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."
"2941","[AI-translation] On the authority of Mu'adh: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: There is no Muslim who goes to bed in a state of purity while remembering (Allah), then wakes up during the night and asks Allah for any good of (the affairs of) this world and the Hereafter, except that He gives it to him."
"2942","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her: What prevents you from listening to what I advise you (with)? That you say when you enter the morning and when you enter the evening: O Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy I seek help. And rectify for me all my affairs, and do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, ever."
"2943","[AI-translation] On the authority of Jarir who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, passed by some women and greeted them with peace."
"2944","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah, marfu'an: Mu'aqqibat, whose utterer or doer will not be disappointed after every obligatory prayer: thirty-three tasbihat, thirty-three tahmidat, and thirty-four takbirat."
"2945","[AI-translation] Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam, marfu'an: Whoever loves that his scroll should delight him, let him abound therein in istighfar."
"2946","On the authority of Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque while he was between Abu Bakr and Umar. And there was Ibn Mas'ud praying, and he was reciting (Surah) An-Nisa'. When he reached the end of the hundred (verses), Ibn Mas'ud began to supplicate while standing in prayer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Ask, you shall be given; ask, you shall be given."" Then he said: ""Whoever wishes to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."" When morning came, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went to him to give him glad tidings and said to him: ""What did you ask Allah for last night?"" He said: ""I said: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not revert, and bliss that does not perish, and the companionship of Muhammad in the highest Paradise of eternity."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and it was said to him: ""Abu Bakr has preceded you!"" He said: ""May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr; I have never been preceded by him to any good except that he preceded me to it."""
"2947","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'A'ishah, marfu'an: Whoever takes the first seven of the Qur'an, he is a hibr."
"2948","[AI-translation] Darda' that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a bow (qaws) for teaching the Qur'an, Allah will collar him with a bow of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"2949","[AI-translation] On the authority of Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) granted permission for the ruqyah of the snake for Banu 'Amr. Abu al-Zubayr said: I heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah saying: A scorpion stung a man among us while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), so a man said: O Messenger of Allah! Shall I perform ruqyah? He said: Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"2950","[AI-translation] Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, marfu'an: Whoever resorts to cauterization or ruqyah has absolved himself of tawakkul."
"2951","[AI-translation] Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs wudu then says: ""Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You,"" it is written in a parchment (raqq), then sealed with a seal, and it will not be broken until the Day of Resurrection."
"2952","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: Whoever enters any of the marketplaces and says: ""There is no god but Allah, alone, having no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,"" Allah writes for him a million good deeds and erases from him a million bad deeds."
"2953","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: Whoever I am mentioned in his presence and he neglects to invoke blessings upon me, has missed the path to Paradise."
"2954","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees one afflicted and says: ""Praise be to Allah who has spared me what He afflicted you with, and favored me above many of those He created with a marked favor,"" that affliction will not befall him."
"2955","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Whoever glorifies Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, praises Allah thirty-three times, and magnifies Allah thirty-three times, that is ninety-nine. Then he said to complete the hundred: ""None has the right to be worshipped but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is able to do all things,"" his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"2956","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud), raised to the Prophet: Whoever is pleased that Allah and His Messenger love him, let him read in the Mus-haf."
"2957","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Whoever is pleased that Allah respond to him during times of hardship and distress, let him supplicate abundantly during times of ease."
"2958","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: Whoever is pleased to look at the Day of Resurrection as if seeing it with his own eyes, let him read ""When the sun is wrapped up,"" ""When the sky is split open,"" and ""When the sky breaks apart."
"2959","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever invokes blessings upon me once, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, records for him ten good deeds."
"2960","[AI-translation] Ansari from his father he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of my Ummah invokes blessings upon me sincerely from his heart, Allah will invoke blessings upon him ten times, raise him ten degrees, record ten good deeds for him, and erase ten evil deeds from him."
"2961","[AI-translation] Juhani: A group came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, so he pledged allegiance to nine and withheld from one. They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You pledged allegiance to nine and left this one?"" He said: ""He has an amulet on him."" So he inserted his hand and cut it, then pledged allegiance to him and said: ""Whoever wears an amulet has committed Shirk."
"2962","[AI-translation] Ashja'i from his father (Tariq bin Ashim) he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever teaches a verse from the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, its reward will be for him as long as it is recited."
"2963","[AI-translation] Mundhir, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, and he used to reside in Ifriqiya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: Whoever says in the morning: ""I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet,"" I am the guarantor to take him by the hand until I enter him into Paradise."
"2964","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever says when he retires to his bed: 'Praise be to Allah Who has sufficed me and given me refuge, praise be to Allah Who has fed me and given me drink, praise be to Allah Who has bestowed favor upon me and given me abundance. O Allah! I ask You by Your Might to save me from the Fire,' he has indeed praised Allah with all the praises of the entire creation."
"2965","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no god, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence, and I repent to Him' three times, his sins are forgiven, even if he had fled from the battlefield."" This has been narrated from the hadith of ........ and al-Bara' bin 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"2966","[AI-translation] Farsi said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: 'O Allah! I bear witness to You, and to Your angels, and the bearers of Your Throne, and to all who are in the heavens and all who are in the earth, that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and messenger' — whoever says it once, Allah frees a third of him from the Fire; whoever says it twice, Allah frees two-thirds of him from the Fire; and whoever says it three times, Allah frees all of him from the Fire."
"2967","[AI-translation] Ansari reported from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Whoever says when he enters the morning: 'There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, He gives life and death, and He has power over all things' ten times, Allah records for him for each time he says it ten good deeds, wipes away from him ten bad deeds, and raises him by ten degrees. And it is for him like freeing ten slaves, and it is a protection for him from the beginning of the day until its end, and he will not perform any deed that day that surpasses them. And if he says it when he enters the evening, then it is the same."
"2968","[AI-translation] Khudri reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Whoever says: 'I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad as my messenger,' Paradise becomes obligatory for him."
"2969","[AI-translation] From Jabir, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah the Almighty and by His praise,' a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."
"2970","[AI-translation] From Jubayr bin Mut'im, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah and by His praise, glory be to You, O Allah, and by Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You' — if he says it in a gathering of remembrance, it is like a seal stamped upon it, and whoever says it in a gathering of vain talk, it is an expiation for him."
"2971","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest,' Allah plants a tree for him in Paradise for each one of them."
"2972","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever says after the morning prayer: 'There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, He gives life and death, and in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things' one hundred times while his legs are folded, he will be on that day the best in deed among the people of the earth, except for one who says the like of what he said or adds to what he said."
"2973","[AI-translation] From Amr bin Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Whoever says in a day two hundred times (one hundred in the morning and one hundred in the evening): 'There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things' — no one who came before him will precede him, and no one who comes after him will catch him, except for one who does a deed better than his deed."
"2974","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever says: 'There is no god but Allah,' it saves him for a day of the age; whatever afflicted him before that, afflicted him."
"2975","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Whoever says: ""There is no deity but Allah, alone, without partner. His is the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is over all things competent,"" ten times after praying the morning prayer, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will record for him ten good deeds, erase from him ten bad deeds, and raise him ten degrees, and it will be equivalent to freeing two slaves from the descendants of Isma'il. If he says it when evening comes, it will be the same for him, and it will be a barrier against Shaytan until the morning."
"2976","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever reads a letter from the Book of Allah will have a good deed by it, and a good deed is multiplied by ten. I do not say that Alif Lam Mim is one letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter."
"2977","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever reads Surah al-Kahf (as it was revealed), it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection from his standing place to Makkah. And whoever reads the last ten verses of it, and then the Dajjal emerges, he will not be harmed. And whoever performs ablution and says: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. (I bear witness that) there is no deity but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You,' it will be written on a parchment, then placed in a seal, and it will not be broken until the Day of Resurrection."
"2978","[AI-translation] From 'Imran bin Husain that he passed by a reciter who was reciting, then he asked (for something). So he asked him to repeat, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) saying: ""Whoever reads the Quran, let him ask Allah by it, for there will come a people who read the Quran and ask the people by it."
"2979","[AI-translation] Juhani from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: Whoever reads ""Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad"" until he completes it ten times, Allah will build for him a palace in Paradise. So 'Umar said: ""Then we will have many palaces, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Allah is more and better."
"2980","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Whoever sits in a sitting place where he does not remember Allah, it will be upon him as a loss from Allah. And whoever lies down in a resting place where he does not remember Allah, it will be upon him as a loss from Allah."
"2981","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Whoever does not call upon Allah, Exalted is He, He becomes angry with him."
"2982","On the authority of Thawbān, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: A Bedouin guest alighted with us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat before his dwellings and began asking him about the people: how was their joy in Islam, and how was their dedication to the prayer? He continued to inform him of that which pleased him until I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ become radiant.When midday arrived and it was time for the meal, he called me secretly, sparing no effort, saying: ""Go to ʿĀʾishah and inform her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has a guest."" She said: ""By Him Who sent him with guidance and the religion of truth, I have nothing in my hand this morning for anyone among the people to eat."" So he sent me back to his wives; all of them excused themselves with the same excuse ʿĀʾishah had given. I saw the complexion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change (turn pale).The Bedouin said: ""We people of the desert are afflicted in our time; we are not people of the settled lands. A handful of dates, over which milk or water is drunk, constitutes abundance for us.""At that moment, a she-goat of ours passed by that had been milked; we used to call it ""Thumar Thumar."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it by its name, ""Thumar Thumar,"" and it came to him humming. He took hold of its leg saying ""Bismillāh,"" then tethered it saying ""Bismillāh,"" then wiped its udder saying ""Bismillāh,"" whereupon it became full of milk.He called for a milking vessel; I brought it to him. He milked into it saying ""Bismillāh"" until he filled it. He handed it to the guest, who drank a large draught. When he wanted to set it down, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""Drink more (ʿUll)."" He wanted to set it down again, and he said to him: ""Drink more."" He kept repeating this to him until he had his fill and drank as much as Allah willed.Then he milked again saying ""Bismillāh"" and filled it, and said: ""Convey this to ʿĀʾishah."" She drank from it whatever she wished. Then I returned to him; he milked into it saying ""Bismillāh,"" then sent me with it to his wives. Whenever one of them drank from it, I returned it to him; he would milk again saying ""Bismillāh"" and fill it, until he said: ""Give it to the guest."" I gave it to him. He said: ""Bismillāh,"" and drank from it whatever Allah willed, then gave it to me. I could not refrain from placing my lips upon the spot of his lips, and I drank a drink sweeter than honey and more fragrant than musk.Then he said: ""O Allah, bless its people in it."""
"2983","[AI-translation] Ash'ari who said: A Surah was revealed and then lifted, and I memorized from it: ""If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third..."" ...to the end of the hadith."
"2984","Anas ibn Malik narrated from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: ""Nothing has troubled my mind since I embraced Islam except that I recited a verse and another person recited it differently from my recitation. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me this verse.' And my companion said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me this verse.' So we went to him and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Did you teach me such-and-such a verse?' He said: 'Yes.' And my companion said: 'Did you teach me such-and-such?' He said: 'Yes.' Gabriel and Michael came to me, so Gabriel sat on my right and Michael on my left. He said: 'Recite on one mode.' Michael said: 'Ask for more.' He said: 'Recite the Qur'an on two modes.' (He said: 'Ask for more') until it reached seven modes. (He said:) 'And each is sufficient and healing.'"""
"2985","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: We said on the day of the Trench (Khandaq): ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there anything we can say, for the hearts have reached the throats?"" He said: ""Yes: O Allah, conceal our faults and secure our fears."" He said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, struck the faces of His enemies with the wind, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, defeated them with the wind."
"2986","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet (peace be upon him) regarding His saying: (""Unquestionably, the allies of Allah will have no fear upon them, nor will they grieve"" (Yunus)), he said: They are those who remember Allah for their seeing [Him]."
"2987","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Jabir bin Abd Allah that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was asked about al-Nushrah. He said: It is from the work of the Shaytan."
"2988","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah, there is no rank above it, so ask Allah to grant me Al-Wasilah."
"2989","[AI-translation] From Abd Allah bin Amr, raised to the Prophet: Do not argue about the Quran, for arguing in it is disbelief."
"2990","[AI-translation] From Ubayy bin Ka'b, raised to the Prophet: Do not curse the wind, and if you see what you dislike, say: O Allah, we ask You for the good of this wind, the good of what is in it, and the good of what it has been commanded to do, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this wind, the evil of what is in it, and the evil of what it has been commanded to do."
"2991","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Do not curse the Shaytan, and seek refuge in Allah from his evil."
"2992","[AI-translation] From Salman, raised to the Prophet: Nothing repels divine decree except supplication, and nothing increases lifespan except righteousness."
"2993","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Four categories of people will be brought on the Day of Resurrection: the newborn child, the insane person, the one who died during the interval between prophets, and the very old person who has lost his mental faculties. All of them will speak with their argument. Then the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will say to a neck of the Fire: 'Come forth.' Then He will say to them: 'I used to send Messengers to My servants from among themselves, and I am the Messenger of Myself to you. Enter this.' Then the one upon whom misery has been decreed will say: 'O Lord! Where shall we enter it, and from it we used to flee?' And the one upon whom happiness has been decreed will proceed and plunge into it swiftly. Then the Blessed and Exalted will say: 'You were more severe in denying and disobeying My Messengers.' So these will enter Paradise and these will enter the Fire."""
"2994","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu Dharr said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The wealthy people have taken all the rewards. They pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast, and they have surplus wealth which they give in charity, but we have no wealth to give in charity."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""O Abu Dharr! Shall I not teach you some words by which you will catch up with those who have preceded you, and no one will surpass you except one who does the same as you? You say 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is Most Great) thirty-three times, and 'Alhamdulillah' (Praise be to Allah) thirty-three times, and 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times, after every prayer, and you conclude with: 'La ilaha illa Allah wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahu al-mulk wa lahu al-hamd wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He is over all things competent). Your sins will be forgiven, even if they were like the foam of the sea."""
"2995","[AI-translation] Juhani that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to him: O Ibn Abis! Shall I not inform you of the best thing with which those who seek refuge take refuge? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak, and Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind - these two surahs."
"2996","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Umm Rafi', may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: O Messenger of Allah! Guide me to a deed for which Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, will reward me. He said: O Umm Rafi'! When you stand for prayer, glorify Allah ten times, proclaim His Oneness ten times, praise Him ten times, magnify Him ten times, and seek His forgiveness ten times. For when you glorify ten times, He says: This is for Me; and when you proclaim His Oneness, He says: This is for Me; and when you praise Him, He says: This is for Me; and when you magnify Him, He says: This is for Me; and when you seek forgiveness, He says: I have forgiven you."
"2997","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Damrah bin Tha'labah: That he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, wearing two garments from the garments of Yemen. He said: O Damrah! Do you think your two garments will admit you to Paradise? He said: If you seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah! I will not sit until I remove them from myself. So the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: O Allah, forgive Damrah bin Tha'labah. So he went off quickly until he removed them from himself."
"2998","'Uqbah ibn 'Amir said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: ""O 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir! Maintain ties with the one who severs ties with you, give to the one who deprives you, and pardon the one who wrongs you."" He said: Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: ""O 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir! Restrain your tongue, weep over your sin, and let your house suffice you."" He said: Then I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: ""O 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir! Shall I not teach you surahs the like of which have not been revealed in the Torah, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Criterion (Qur'an)? No night shall come upon you except that you recite them in it."" (Surah al-Ikhlas, Surah al-Falaq, Surah an-Nas)"
"2999","[AI-translation] Abbas: O uncle, make abundant supplication for well-being."
"3000","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to say: ""O Guardian of Islam and its people, keep me firm in it until I meet You."
"3001","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to say: ""O Guardian of Islam and its people, make me firm in Islam until I meet You upon it."
"3002","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, attributed to the Prophet ﷺ: The Quran will come on the Day of Resurrection like a pale man, saying to its companion: ""Do you recognize me? I am the one who used to keep you awake at night and make you thirsty at midday. Every merchant is behind his merchandise, but I am for you today behind every merchant."" So he will be given the dominion in his right hand and eternity in his left, and a crown of dignity will be placed on his head. His parents will be clothed in two garments the like of which the world and what is in it cannot equal. They will say: ""O Lord! From where do we have this?"" It will be said: ""By your teaching your child the Quran."" And the companion of the Quran will be told on the Day of Resurrection: ""Recite and ascend in the ranks, and recite distinctly as you used to recite in the world, for your abode is at the last verse you recite."""
"3003","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, elevated to the Prophet: It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an, ""Read, ascend, and recite carefully as you used to recite carefully in the world, for your station is at the last verse you recite."
